		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2854&amp;p=24598#p24598"><![CDATA[
Good afternoon, after updating the latest firmware, the equipment did not turn on anymore and does not enter programming mode. Does anyone have a solution to this problem or it only remains to occupy it as a paperweight, thank you very much in advance 73s<br>Tried the battery and nothing<br><br>Edit<br><br>Happy ending, <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"> <br><br>despair was stronger than sanity... the boot mode is not damaged, but the structure is changed. I managed to recover it in the following way: remove the battery from the radio, press the 3 side buttons plus the upper one and reinsert the radio. With this, the green light came on and the computer recognized the radio. to bring it back to life, I used an old firmware updater and an old version of dm1801 and voila! <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy">  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy">  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2362">cx8anm</a> — Mon Jul 24, 2023 4:06 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
